<!--
  Example swing-leg-controller stage plugins (issue #17, M4.2).

  base_class_type: StagePlugin<SwingLegControllerInterface>
    (mit_controller/stage_plugin.hpp + mit_controller/swing_leg_controller_interface.hpp)

  This file is the out-of-package twin of controllers' plugins/slc_plugins.xml.
  It declares the same base string, is registered against the same ament resource
  (`controllers__pluginlib__plugin`, see CMakeLists.txt), and is found by the same
  StageLoader — the only difference is that it ships from another package
  entirely, which is what M4.2 exists to demonstrate.

  The '<' in base_class_type is XML-escaped as &lt;/&gt; (stage_loading.md §5).

  `path` is the CMake target name WITHOUT a `lib` prefix. This is the one place
  this file deliberately differs from controllers' stock description XMLs, which
  all spell it `libmpc_plugins`-style: pluginlib accepts both but warns
  ("given plugin name 'libX' should be 'X' for better portability") on the
  prefixed form, because the prefix is platform-specific. A file people are meant
  to copy should not seed a warning into every package that copies it.


  The `example_` prefix on the id is deliberate: this stage makes the robot stand,
  not walk, and the selected `slc.type` value should say so wherever it is read
  (README.md §1).
-->
<class_libraries>
  <library path="example_slc_plugins">
    <class name="example_passthrough_slc"
           type="example_stage_plugins::PassthroughSlcPlugin"
           base_class_type="StagePlugin&lt;SwingLegControllerInterface&gt;">
      <description>
        Demo/diagnostic swing leg controller: holds every foot at its current
        position (identity/passthrough) and optionally logs the scheduled leg
        states at a throttled rate. Not production locomotion — the robot stands
        and does not step. See this package's README.md.
      </description>
    </class>
  </library>
</class_libraries>
